                                "sense_id": "320c7414-51ec-3fa6-8fbe-fa3cf8f1ea70",
                                "text": "The clear winners in this cynical charade were the Clintonoid Democrats, who (as well as being hardened to switching and shifting between elitism and populism) could supply the most cobwebbed rules-monger on one hand—the aforementioned Senator Byrd—and the most sinuous arguments of the short-term general will on the other."
